{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "ASV1901",
  "book_code": "PRO",
  "chapter": 16,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PRO.16.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.16.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The plans of the heart belong to man;\nBut the answer of the tongue is from Jehovah.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.16.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.16.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "All the ways of a man are clean in his own eyes;\nBut Jehovah weigheth the spirits.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.16.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.16.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Commit thy works unto Jehovah,\nAnd thy purposes shall be established.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.16.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.16.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Jehovah hath made everything for its own end;\nYea, even the wicked for the day of evil.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.16.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.16.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Every one that is proud in heart is an abomination to Jehovah:",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "Though",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " hand ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "join",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in hand, he shall not be unpunished.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.16.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.16.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "By mercy and truth iniquity is atoned for;\nAnd by the fear of Jehovah men depart from evil.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.16.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.16.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When a man’s ways please Jehovah,\nHe maketh even his enemies to be at peace with him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.16.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.16.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Better is a little, with righteousness,\nThan great revenues with injustice.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.16.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.16.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A man’s heart deviseth his way;\nBut Jehovah directeth his steps.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.16.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.16.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A divine sentence is in the lips of the king;\nHis mouth shall not transgress in judgment.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.16.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.16.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A just balance and scales are Jehovah’s;\nAll the weights of the bag are his work.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.16.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.16.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "It is an abomination to kings to commit wickedness;\nFor the throne is established by righteousness.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.16.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.16.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Righteous lips are the delight of kings;\nAnd they love him that speaketh right.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.16.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.16.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The wrath of a king is ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " messengers of death;\nBut a wise man will pacify it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.16.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.16.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "In the light of the king’s countenance is life;\nAnd his favor is as a cloud of the latter rain.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.16.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.16.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "How much better is it to get wisdom than gold!\nYea, to get understanding is rather to be chosen than silver.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.16.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.16.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The highway of the upright is to depart from evil:\nHe that keepeth his way preserveth his soul.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.16.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.16.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Pride ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "goeth",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " before destruction,\nAnd a haughty spirit before a fall.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.16.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.16.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Better it is to be of a lowly spirit with the poor,\nThan to divide the spoil with the proud.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.16.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.16.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He that giveth heed unto the word shall find good;\nAnd whoso trusteth in Jehovah, happy is he.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.16.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.16.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The wise in heart shall be called prudent;\nAnd the sweetness of the lips increaseth learning.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.16.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.16.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Understanding is a well-spring of life unto him that hath it;\nBut the correction of fools is ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "their",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " folly.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.16.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.16.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The heart of the wise instructeth his mouth,\nAnd addeth learning to his lips.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.16.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.16.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Pleasant words are ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a honeycomb,\nSweet to the soul, and health to the bones.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.16.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.16.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "There is a way which seemeth right unto a man,\nBut the end thereof are the ways of death.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.16.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.16.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The appetite of the laboring man laboreth for him;\nFor his mouth urgeth him ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "thereto",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.16.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.16.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A worthless man deviseth mischief;\nAnd in his lips there is as a scorching fire.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.16.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.16.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A perverse man scattereth abroad strife;\nAnd a whisperer separateth chief friends.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.16.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.16.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A man of violence enticeth his neighbor,\nAnd leadeth him in a way that is not good.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.16.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.16.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He that shutteth his eyes, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to devise perverse things:\nHe that compresseth his lips bringeth evil to pass.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.16.31",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.16.31",
      "verse": 31,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The hoary head is a crown of glory;It shall be found in the way of righteousness.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.16.32",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.16.32",
      "verse": 32,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He that is slow to anger is better than the mighty;\nAnd he that ruleth his spirit, than he that taketh a city.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.16.33",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.16.33",
      "verse": 33,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The lot is cast into the lap;\nBut the whole disposing thereof is of Jehovah.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    }
  ]
}
